15:54.804 --> 15:57.814
I love my wife! I want her back!

16:06.415 --> 16:08.915
All aboard?

16:13.255 --> 16:14.456
[ALAN HUMMlNG]

16:14.457 --> 16:17.527
Sweetie? Uh, you're humming again.

16:17.760 --> 16:19.761
Sorry. Don't know the words.

16:19.762 --> 16:22.262
[CHUCKLES]

16:25.534 --> 16:31.064
Um, okay, uh-- Could you please
not open your mouth so wide?

16:32.241 --> 16:33.775
ALAN:
Better now?

16:33.776 --> 16:35.677
Uh, yeah, it's fine. Just, uh...

16:35.678 --> 16:38.146
...can you not talk in my mouth?

16:38.147 --> 16:41.850
Wow, ha, ha. More rules than
a public pool around here, ha, ha.

16:41.851 --> 16:45.987
They're not rules. It's just, uh,
I know what I like and you're not doing it.

16:45.988 --> 16:49.090
- All right, fine. What do you like, Judith?
- I have to tell you?

16:49.091 --> 16:52.026
- No, no. Let me guess and get yelled at.
- Nobody's yelling at you.

16:52.027 --> 16:53.828
- I'm not your mother.
- Oh, you're right.

16:53.829 --> 16:57.399
My mother can emasculate me
without raising her voice.

16:57.400 --> 16:58.967
Oh, God, I can't do this.

16:58.968 --> 17:01.536
- Do what?
- I can't be with you again.

17:01.537 --> 17:04.472
I was afraid of being 40 years old
and all by myself...

17:04.473 --> 17:09.844
...but dying alone has gotta be better
than being stuck with you.

17:09.845 --> 17:12.147
Now you're starting to sound
like my mother.

17:12.148 --> 17:13.348
[KNOCKlNG ON DOOR]

17:13.349 --> 17:16.284
HERB:
Judith! I love you! Please take me back!

17:16.285 --> 17:18.785
Oh, boy, this is awkward.

17:18.821 --> 17:20.655
Coming, darling!

17:20.656 --> 17:23.156
Get out of here.

17:23.793 --> 17:26.828
Oh, uh, just so we're clear,
we've decided to see other people?

17:26.829 --> 17:29.329
Get out!

17:32.668 --> 17:34.669
Thanks for the ride, girls.

17:34.670 --> 17:37.170
And for bringing me home.

17:39.542 --> 17:43.011
[SlNGlNG]
I've been working on the railroad

17:43.012 --> 17:46.004
All the livelong day

17:46.182 --> 17:49.851
Dinah, won't you blow
Dinah, won't you blow, Di--

17:49.852 --> 17:52.878
- Hey, Alan.
- Hey.

17:53.055 --> 17:54.489
Mind if I join you?

17:54.490 --> 17:55.924
It's your house.

17:55.925 --> 17:58.425
Oh, yeah.

17:58.494 --> 18:02.191
Excuse me. Pardon me, hot soup.

18:06.502 --> 18:09.002
What the hell?

18:12.775 --> 18:15.343
Well, that's a little embarrassing.

18:15.344 --> 18:16.544
What is that?

18:16.545 --> 18:19.045
A railroad-crossing sign.

18:19.181 --> 18:21.382
Sorry, I need more.

18:21.383 --> 18:24.393
I was having sex on a train set.

18:24.887 --> 18:29.324
How else do you get a crossing sign
stuck to your ass?

18:29.325 --> 18:30.692
Of course.

18:30.693 --> 18:32.160
Hey, it could've been worse.

18:32.161 --> 18:34.496
I could've had a caboose in my caboose.

18:34.497 --> 18:36.264
[LAUGHlNG]

18:36.265 --> 18:38.765
Oh, come on, that's funny.

18:39.168 --> 18:41.236
[CHUCKLES lNSlNCERELY]

18:41.237 --> 18:43.905
What happened when Herb showed up
at Judith's house?

18:43.906 --> 18:47.509
- How did you know about that?
- Lucky guess.

18:47.510 --> 18:48.710
[SlGHS]

18:48.711 --> 18:50.712
She kicked me out again, Charlie.

18:50.713 --> 18:53.882
I had to sneak out her back door
while she threw herself into Herb's arms.

18:53.883 --> 18:56.383
[LAUGHS]

18:56.719 --> 19:00.289
- What's so funny?
- You said back door.

19:00.456 --> 19:03.496
It reminds me of my caboose joke.

19:04.660 --> 19:06.928
Good night.

19:06.929 --> 19:08.763
I'm here all week.

19:08.764 --> 19:11.264
Tip your waitresses.

19:21.176 --> 19:22.644
Hey, Mom? It's Charlie.

19:22.645 --> 19:24.646
Yeah, I know it's late. Listen.

19:24.647 --> 19:27.157
Do you think this is funny?

19:30.019 --> 19:33.318
Huh. Must've got disconnected.

19:38.027 --> 19:40.527
Hey, Jake. You sleeping?

19:47.670 --> 19:48.870
[DOORBELL RlNGS]

19:48.871 --> 19:50.371
- Doorbell.
- Doorbell!

19:50.372 --> 19:52.872
ALAN:
Coming!

19:59.848 --> 20:03.551
- Oh. Oh, hi. Thanks for bringing him over.
- Oh, no problem.

20:03.552 --> 20:06.621
- Hey, guess what?
- Herb, why don't we let Jake tell him.

20:06.622 --> 20:08.957
- Uh, tell me what?
- Jake?

20:08.958 --> 20:14.488
My grades aren't good enough
for military school, so ha, ha.

20:15.197 --> 20:17.065
No, sweetheart, the other thing.

20:17.066 --> 20:21.376
Oh, I'm gonna have
a little brother or sister.

20:22.504 --> 20:24.038
You're-- You're pregnant?

20:24.039 --> 20:27.508
Yes, Alan.
Herb and I are going to have a baby.

20:27.509 --> 20:29.010
Congratulations.

20:29.011 --> 20:33.321
Try to keep this one
away from the lead paint.

20:33.749 --> 20:35.383
Did you hear that, Alan?

20:35.384 --> 20:41.222
They've only been back together six weeks
and they're gonna have a baby.

20:41.223 --> 20:43.291
I heard.

20:43.292 --> 20:46.694
- Come in, we'll pop a bottle of champagne.
- Aah, champagne.

20:46.695 --> 20:49.664
Uh, no. We really should be going.
Come on, Herb.

20:49.665 --> 20:52.165
- Goodbye.
- Oh, shoot.

20:52.801 --> 20:55.895
What a remarkable coincidence.

20:56.071 --> 20:57.839
Yeah, coincidence.

20:57.840 --> 21:00.340
- You okay?
- No.

21:00.476 --> 21:02.777
Come on, let's sit you down.

21:02.778 --> 21:05.278
Yeah. Let's sit me down.

21:07.216 --> 21:09.017
Here you go, buddy.

21:09.018 --> 21:11.518
Here I go.

21:12.621 --> 21:14.856
What's wrong with him?

21:14.857 --> 21:17.587
He's doing math in his head.

21:18.193 --> 21:20.693
Oh, yeah, that's a bitch.
